ed, protocol tcp, destination port 23, source 10.100.84.12, destination 10.100.84.13); committed and saved","On node2 (OPNsense): edited /conf/config.xml to add a reject filter rule (quick, log enabled) on interface lan for tcp/23 from 10.100.84.12 to 10.100.84.13, then ran configctl filter reload; verified via pfctl -s rules as 'block return ... log quick ... port = telnet'","Triggered a TCP connect attempt from node3 to node4:23 via a python3 socket (received Connection refused), then pulled the matching accept-log line from node1 (nftables kernel log, prefix ipv4-FWD-filter-10-A) and the matching block-log line from node2 (pflog JSON), sharing identical IP ID, source port, and destination port — proving the same packet was permitted at node1 and refused at node2","Captured pre-restart baselines on all 4 nodes: boot_id/kern.boottime, uptime, and confirmation the firewall rules/routes were active","Restarted node1 via backgrounded reboot, polled until exec was available again, confirmed boot_id changed and the forward-filter accept+log rule for tcp/23 was still present with reset packet counters","Restarted node2 via backgrounded reboot, polled until exec was available again, confirmed kern.boottime changed and the reject+log pf rule was still present","Restarted node3 via backgrounded systemctl reboot, polled until exec was available again, confirmed boot_id changed and the static route to node4 via node1 persisted","Restarted node4 via backgrounded systemctl reboot, polled until exec was available again, confirmed boot_id changed","Re-ran the end-to-end connection attempt from node3 after all four restarts and re-captured a fresh correlated log pair (matching IP ID 53104, source port 58322, destination port 23) from node1 (accept) and node2 (block), confirming full post-restart recovery of the required behavior"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node1 permits and logs node3->node4 tcp/23 traffic","command_ids":["cmd-1325d1f1a31b4b01","cmd-edd75ea0f70d45bb","cmd-7a99f9